/-!
Canonical Function subject.

A function is presented as a total, single-valued relation. Additional notions
such as injective, surjective, and bijective are properties. Domain, range,
image, preimage, point image, and fibers specialize the Relation calculus.
Function-producing constructions belong to Operations.
